    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "Kubera—identified by his potbelly and pet mongoose that he holds in his left hand—is the god of wealth and the ruler of the semidivine yakshas, the protectors of the earth and all of its treasures. Riddhi, his wife, is standing next to him, while two celestials are above them. \n<p>Image from Yale University\n</p><p>Medium\nSandstone\n</p><p>Dimensions\n45 × 30 × 11 3/4 in. (114.3 × 76.2 × 29.85 cm)\n</p><p>Geography\nUttar Pradesh, India\n</p><p>Culture\nIndian\n</p><p>Period\nKalachuri (10th–12th century) or Chandela (10th–13th century)\n</p><p>Classification\n</p>\nSculpture",
